## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public Netlify
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- Migration numbering is authoritative: Phase 11 = admitted AI extensions,
  Phase 12 = Club/Community, Phase 13 = Cutover.
- `origin/main` is `a3ee7ae2db196f498085979f3a643f00b70e43f7` (after PR #73).
- Work branch `feat/price-intelligence-1a-foundation` carries four commits from
  that SHA, head `ac6a0e953b0440794ce703a418cd378429084cdd`, open as PR #74
  toward `main`. The PR touches exactly eight files and does not contain
  `.wslconfig`, which is pre-existing local work and was left untracked.
- Price Intelligence 1A adds one migration,
  `supabase/migrations/20260824120000_price_intelligence_1a_observations.sql`,
  which has **not** been applied to any Supabase project. It creates
  `public.wine_price_observations` (append-only history), enums
  `price_observation_tipo` (`richiesta`, `vendita`) and
  `price_observation_fonte` (single label `vinea_interno`), the read view
  `public.wine_price_history`, three append-only triggers, one write door
  `private.price_observation_registra`, and two domain triggers.
- ASKING is a trigger on `public.listings`, not an RPC, because since
  `20260819090000_annuncio_modifica_attivo.sql` a seller UPDATEs
  `prezzo_cents` directly through PostgREST and at least six code paths write
  `stato = 'attivo'`. The `riservato` -> `attivo` return is the one deliberate
  exclusion: it is written by reservation-release paths on checkout expiry and
  is not a new quotation.
- SALE is a trigger on `public.orders` firing on the transition to `completato`,
  reached by four existing paths, with price `orders.prezzo_cents` frozen on the
  order. `completato` is **not** absorbing: `public.ordine_contesta` accepts it
  among contestable states while payout has not transferred, so
  `completato -> contestato -> completato` is the ordinary dispute-resolution
  path. A `vendita` row therefore means "this order reached `completato` at this
  price", not "this money can never come back"; re-entry writes no second row
  and a later refund alters nothing. Weighting refunds statistically is a 1B
  decision.
- `anon` and `authenticated` have no privilege on the base table and read only
  through the view. `service_role` deliberately keeps its GRANT, exactly as on
  `audit_log`: rewrite, deletion and external source are closed by three
  triggers and a row CHECK, which bind privileged writers too.
- The grid `supabase/tests/price_intelligence_1a.sql` was really executed on
  2026-08-24 on a disposable PostgreSQL 17.10 container, from empty, bootstrap
  `9c` plus 36 migrations each in its own transaction. First clean run
  **27 PASSA / 2 FALLISCE**; after correction **30 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**; after
  the VERIFY audit added cases 31-32, **32 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**, with zero
  fixture residue. It was not run against production.
- Of the two original failures, case 21 was a defect in the grid (column
  expectation mis-sorted) and case 27 was a false claim in the migration comment
  about `service_role`'s privileges. Cases 31-32 came from a reading during the
  VERIFY audit, not from a failure: they assert that leaving and re-entering
  `completato` writes no second `vendita`.
- `frontend-next` gains a read-only contract `PriceIntelligenceService` in
  `src/services/types.ts` and the adapter
  `src/services/price-intelligence/supabase-price-intelligence-service.ts`,
  which reads the view and never the base table and has no write method.
  No UI consumes it: charts, ranges, suggested price and `/vendi` are 1B.
- VERIFY on `frontend-next` was green: lint 0 errors / 14 pre-existing warnings,
  typecheck clean, **681 tests pass / 0 fail**, production build green,
  `git diff --check` clean. `MIN_TESTS` was raised 669 -> 681 in
