## BLOCKERS / NOTES

- The migration has never run on production. The backfill's effect on real data
  is unmeasured: how many active listings it will convert into `richiesta`
  observations is known only for the disposable database.
- The grid does not cover PostgREST: it proves `authenticated` cannot write in
  SQL, not that the browser receives the correct `403`. It also proves sale
  idempotency against a repetition, not against two simultaneous completions;
  that case rests on the partial unique index alone.
- `wine_price_history` is a `security_invoker = off` view, so the Supabase
  linter will report `security_definer_view`. It is the expected signal, the
  same as for `public_listings` and `public_clubs`.
- The 12b and 12d grids are absent from `supabase/tests/README.md`. That gap
  predates this task and was not filled from here.
- No usable authenticated browser session was available. Authenticated
  `/vendite`, the Seller Dashboard and the `quasi` badge over a real photograph
  remain unobserved in a browser.
- The authenticated Home has not been rendered. `Club che segui`, followed-club
  exclusion, empty state and read-error behavior are proven by tests only.
- The authenticated profile-photo smoke remains outstanding: upload, save,
  Account and seller rendering, preset/initials switch and old-object cleanup.
- The authenticated OPEN club-creation flow on production also remains unrun.
- `oltre` (`bg-destructive/20 text-destructive`) remains a translucent badge
  over an unknown photograph. It was outside PR #72 and remains uncorrected.
- The seller dashboard has one data-model gap: no order completion timestamp is
  client-readable, so both temporal series group by month of order receipt.
- The Club 12d grid must not run against production: it writes users, clubs,
  posts, replies, likes, reports and Storage objects. It does not cover
  PostgREST, the browser image pipeline or concurrent same-name creation.
- Phase 11 implementation is not open. A new two-provider F01 canary lacks
  current authorization and paid-project confirmation.
- Phase 13 has not started and must not be inferred from the public beta or
  green checks.
- The embedded Supabase test mailer remains unsuitable for real traffic; custom
  SMTP depends on a verifiable custom domain.
- Before enabling payments, remeasure scheduler configuration and obtain a
  successful fail-closed health run; old failure counts are historical.
- External Price Intelligence providers remain OFF and fail-closed. Turning one
  on requires three explicit acts in a NEW migration — an enum label, the row
  CHECK, and a write path — plus cabin authorization of provider, plan, budget
  and credentials. None of the three can happen by accident.
